description:
Make the repository root a virtual workspace (members crates/*, resolver 3, shared version, inherited lints and dependency versions) and move the package with src, tests, benches, examples, its manifest and its README to crates/frost-collections with git mv. A short workspace README replaces the root README. No Rust source line changes except relative paths.

In the same change:
- repoint every manifest, #[path] include, script, tool configuration, workflow and documentation link in verification/results/crate-split/layout-inventory.tsv that names a moved path; refresh the lockfile of each isolated package whose path dependency moved;
- the Makefile selects packages with -p from cargo metadata and never relies on feature unification at the workspace root;
- the catalog tool checks a workspace: a root catalog for repository tooling plus one catalog per package with package-relative paths, IDs unique across files, contract references across files (decision D11); the package catalog and benchmark inventory move into crates/frost-collections/verification/metadata;
- make package uses the scratch-workspace test of decision D13;
- the link checker covers package documents;
- the one-package policy is replaced by the plan's package list in every document named in section 6 of the plan, marking packages not yet extracted.

Acceptance: git diff -M100% --name-status shows R100 for every file under src, tests, benches and examples except files whose relative paths had to change, which are listed. The union of catalog case IDs is the 397 of the baseline. Gates: make verify, make embedded, make bounded, make loom, make fuzz-check and make doctest-codes pass. Per profile (all-features, default, alloc, core-only, int-set) the multiset of (integration target, passed, ignored) equals the baseline of frost-wlt.7, the unit-test and doctest sums over packages equal the baseline, and failed is 0; any difference is a row of the migration table. cargo tree -e features shows core without std in the alloc, core-only and int-set lanes. CHANGELOG and the migration table in docs/design/crate-split-plan.md are updated in the same change. A lane whose tool is missing is recorded as not run (decision D16).
